---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Surfaces — Chris Buice"
  description="A music tool I built for myself, and what it noticed."
>
  <article class="surfaces" data-page="surfaces">

    <header class="surfaces-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">A project · 2026</p>
      <h1 class="surfaces-title">Surfaces</h1>
    </header>

    <section class="lede" aria-label="Introduction">
      <p>
        Surfaces is a music tool I built for myself. It watches what I'm
        listening to, learns what I've loved before, and surfaces tracks for
        the surfaces of my day &mdash; working music in the morning, something
        quieter at night, something else entirely on a long drive. It talks
        to Spotify, talks to Claude, and talks back to me through Siri when I
        ask it to.
      </p>

      <p>
        I listen. Spotify keeps a record. Surfaces reads it like a book
        &mdash; fifteen years, around 260,000 plays, every one of them logged
        in passing and never really looked at until now. There are patterns
        in there I'd never have spotted on my own. Some are about music.
        Some are about me. The surface, it turns out, is also a mirror.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section class="constellation-section" aria-label="Listening constellation">
      <div class="constellation-frame">
        <!--
          Constellation island lives here.
          Renders ~1,500-node SVG on desktop, 200-node static still on mobile.
          Fetches /api/constellation from the Surfaces worker.
        -->
        <div
          id="constellation-mount"
          class="constellation-mount"
          data-endpoint="https://surfaces.chrisbuice.workers.dev/api/constellation"
          aria-label="A field of dots representing every artist Chris has played more than ten times since 2011."
          role="img"
        >
          <p class="constellation-loading">Generating constellation&hellip;</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <figcaption class="constellation-caption">
        <p class="caption-line">
          Every artist I've played more than ten times since 2011, positioned
          by what I've listened to alongside what.
        </p>
        <p class="caption-meta tnum">
          <span data-meta-generated>Generated nightly</span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <span data-meta-artists>&mdash;&nbsp;artists</span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <span data-meta-edges>&mdash;&nbsp;connections</span>
        </p>
        <p class="caption-mobile-hint">
          On a wider screen this becomes something you can touch &mdash;
          every dot a story.
        </p>
        <p class="caption-meaning">
          Some artists glow steady &mdash; the ones I've returned to year
          after year, the company I keep. Others fade to ghost &mdash; loved
          hard for a season and then never quite again, the way some music
          is meant to belong to a particular stretch of months and nothing
          after.
        </p>
      </figcaption>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section class="numbers" aria-label="Surfaces in numbers">
      <dl class="numbers-grid">
        <div class="number">
          <dt class="number-label">Plays since 2011</dt>
          <dd class="number-value tnum" data-stat-plays>261,000</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="number">
          <dt class="number-label">Unique artists</dt>
          <dd class="number-value tnum" data-stat-artists>1,600</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="number">
          <dt class="number-label">Seasonal playlists since 2016</dt>
          <dd class="number-value tnum" data-stat-seasons>39</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section class="how" aria-label="How it works">
      <h2 class="how-heading">How it works</h2>
      <p>
        The system watches what I play and learns from it. Every night, while
        I sleep, it rebuilds a profile of my taste &mdash; what I'm leaning
        into, what I'm cooling on, what time of day I tend to want what. A
        second program reads music blogs and indie radio feeds, looking for
        new tracks that might fit, and adds the strongest candidates to a
        pool of fresh discoveries. When I want to listen, it draws from both
        sides &mdash; the familiar and the new &mdash; and tunes the mix to
        where I am, what the weather is doing, and what kind of attention I
        have to spare. The whole thing runs on Cloudflare's edge, the same
        network that powers a large fraction of the web, in small bursts
        that wake up when I need them and disappear when I don't. About ten
        thousand lines of TypeScript. Built solo in three days using Claude
        Code.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section class="submit" aria-label="Send me a song">
      <h2 class="submit-heading">Send me a song</h2>
      <p class="submit-blurb">
        If a track has been living in your head and you think it'd live in
        mine too, send it over. It joins the same pool of fresh candidates
        Surfaces pulls from when it builds a session.
      </p>

      <!--
        Submission form island lives here.
        Real Spotify search picker (Pages Function proxies the search API),
        optional 'from' and 'note' fields, posts to /api/submit-track.
      -->
      <div id="submit-mount" class="submit-mount">
        <p class="submit-placeholder">
          The submission tool is coming with the next update.
          For now, email me the track at
          <a href="mailto:chris@chrisbuice.com">chris@chrisbuice.com</a>
          and I'll add it by hand.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="surfaces-foot">
      <p class="foot-links">
        <a href="https://github.com/chrisbuice/surfaces" rel="noopener">
          Source on GitHub
        </a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        <a href="/">Back to chrisbuice.com</a>
      </p>
    </footer>

  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
  /* Page-level register                                                 */
  /* The Base layout caps content at 640px via .content-column, which    */
  /* is right for prose but wrong for the constellation. Override the    */
  /* column for this page so prose stays at reading width but the        */
  /* constellation can breathe.                                          */
  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

  .surfaces {
    /* Wider than the default 640px — the constellation needs room.
       Prose sections re-narrow themselves below. */
    max-width: 960px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-block: var(--space-xl) var(--space-l);
  }

  /* Body-class font swap — /surfaces leans more editorial.
     Targets the article so the change is scoped and additive,
     not destructive of the rest of the site. */
  .surfaces[data-page="surfaces"] p {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: 380;
    font-size: 1.18rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
  /* Header                                                              */
  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

  .surfaces-head {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-l);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-s);
  }

  .surfaces-title {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 5.25rem);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
  /* Lede                                                                */
  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

  .lede {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-l);
  }

  /* The first letter of the first paragraph as a quiet drop cap.
     Felton-register editorial signal. Not a giant decorative cap;
     a small typographic flourish that matches Fraunces. */
  .lede > p:first-of-type::first-letter {
    font-size: 3.6em;
    line-height: 0.85;
    float: left;
    padding-right: 0.08em;
    padding-top: 0.05em;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
  /* Constellation                                                       */
  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

  .constellation-section {
    margin-block: var(--space-l);
  }

  .constellation-frame {
    /* No border, no background, no chart-junk. The constellation floats
       on the page background. Aspect ratio reserved so the page doesn't
       reflow when the SVG arrives. */
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 880px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    position: relative;
  }

  .constellation-mount {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .constellation-loading {
    font-family: var(--font-body) !important;
    font-size: 0.75rem !important;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    color: var(--text-muted) !important;
  }

  /* Caption stack, narrow, asymmetric to the left at wide widths.
     Below the visual on mobile, beside-and-below on desktop. */
  .constellation-caption {
    max-width: 560px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    margin-top: var(--space-m);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .caption-line {
    font-family: var(--font-heading) !important;
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.05rem !important;
    line-height: 1.5 !important;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-s);
  }

  .caption-meta {
    font-family: var(--font-body) !important;
    font-size: 0.7rem !important;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--text-muted) !important;
    line-height: 1.4 !important;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-m);
  }

  .caption-meta > span {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-inline: 0.25em;
  }

  .caption-mobile-hint {
    font-family: var(--font-heading) !important;
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 0.95rem !important;
    color: var(--text-muted) !important;
    line-height: 1.5 !important;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-m);
  }

  /* Hide the mobile hint on screens wide enough for the full experience. */
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .caption-mobile-hint {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  .caption-meaning {
    font-family: var(--font-heading) !important;
    font-size: 1rem !important;
    line-height: 1.55 !important;
    color: var(--text);
    text-align: left;
    /* Intentionally left-aligned while the lines above are centered.
       Mandy-Brown-style asymmetry inside the caption stack — the
       meaning sentence reads like prose, not a label. */
  }

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
  /* Numbers                                                             */
  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

  .numbers {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    margin-block: var(--space-l);
  }

  .numbers-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-m);
    text-align: center;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .numbers-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-s);
    }
  }

  .number {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
  }

  .number-label {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    order: 2;
  }

  .number-value {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.25rem);
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 400;
    order: 1;
  }

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
  /* How it works                                                        */
  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

  .how {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    margin-block: var(--space-l);
  }

  .how-heading,
  .submit-heading {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--font-size-h2);
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-s);
  }

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
  /* Submit                                                              */
  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

  .submit {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    margin-block: var(--space-l);
  }

  .submit-blurb {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-m);
  }

  .submit-mount {
    /* Will be replaced by the real form island.
       For launch, contains the email fallback below. */
  }

  .submit-placeholder {
    font-family: var(--font-body) !important;
    font-size: 0.95rem !important;
    color: var(--text-muted) !important;
    padding: var(--space-m);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 2px;
  }

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
  /* Footer                                                              */
  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

  .surfaces-foot {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    padding-top: var(--space-m);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .foot-links {
    font-family: var(--font-body) !important;
    font-size: 0.8rem !important;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--text-muted) !important;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .foot-links > span {
    margin-inline: 0.5em;
  }
</style>
